# GitHub is the work log

Chats are not the record. Anyone taking over uses GitHub, not this thread. Every real action is documented. Every committable action is committed.

- **Todo = Issue** in `fjdresources/ai-office-frontend`, on Project [fjdr-ai-office](https://github.com/orgs/fjdresources/projects/1). Open or update an Issue for each distinct leftover. A decision with no code yet still gets an Issue. Do not file backend work here.
- **Committable change = branch + commit + PR into `main`.** App code, Cursor rules, `.env.example`, compose, docs. PR body starts with `Fixes #N` (or `Fixes fjdresources/ai-office-backend#N` if the todo is on the other repo). Merge closes the Issue; the Project card goes to Done. Do not push straight to `main` unless the user explicitly says to. See `git-deploy.mdc`.
- **Settings / browser / CDP that cannot go in git** (Coolify, Cloudflare, GitHub UI, live secrets): still document in an Issue (what was clicked, the result) or a committed rule/doc. Never commit secret values.
- **Do not** treat Cursor plan todos or a chat recap as the log. **Do not** put the PR on the board as the todo when an Issue already is.
- **End of a work chat:** leftover = open Issues on the Project; shipped = merged PRs with `Fixes`. If that is missing, open or update the Issue and commit/PR before you stop. Keep `roadmap.mdc` Done/Next aligned with those Issues.

Finishing a real action counts as asking to record it (exception to “only commit when asked”).
